Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Calcula itself is MIT. The computer algebra engine it loads at runtime is not, and
is kept at arm's length for exactly that reason.

Symja / matheclipse — https://github.com/axkr/symja_android_library
    matheclipse-core, matheclipse-parser, matheclipse-external
    GNU Lesser General Public License v3 (LGPL-3.0)

JAS (Java Algebra System) — https://krum.rz.uni-mannheim.de/jas/
    Pulled in transitively by Symja.
    GNU Lesser General Public License

These are NOT linked into the application. They ship as ordinary jars in the
`cas/` directory beside the executable and are loaded through a URLClassLoader at
runtime. A user may replace any of them with a modified build by dropping a
different jar into that directory and restarting — which is how Calcula satisfies
the LGPL's relink requirement.

Source for the versions shipped is available from the upstream projects above.

